# Part of sys-ice: Snowpoint Temple B3F, the ice field (x 2–15, z 7–14). One step onto the ice slides
# the player until the next tile is blocked: down from (3, 6) to (3, 14), right to (15, 14), up to
# (15, 12). Each wait is on the stop tile, then 20 ticks prove the slide stopped there. The `ice-*`
# screenshot lines are the browser spec's key beat (the view moved with the slide, the player drawn).
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_SNOWPOINT_TEMPLE_B3F 3 6 down
until idle
+0 screenshot ice-start
+0 press down
+1 release down
until position 3 14 120
+20 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_SNOWPOINT_TEMPLE_B3F 3 14
+0 screenshot ice-stop
+0 press right
until position 4 14
+0 release right
until position 15 14 120
+20 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_SNOWPOINT_TEMPLE_B3F 15 14
+0 press up
until position 15 13
+0 release up
until position 15 12 120
+20 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_SNOWPOINT_TEMPLE_B3F 15 12
